vendor/apn: let a product supply its own APN database

LineageOS installs its generated APN list to /product/etc/apns-conf.xml. The vantage image
ships the stock Android 17 list instead (it has the carrier initial-attach and tethering
APNs that the LineageOS list lacks for Optimum 313390, and it is what the Android 16 port
was verified with). Soong writes install rules for every enabled module, so the stock copy
and this module clash in Kati unless this one is disabled; the product sets
lineage_apn.use_device_apns (vantage.mk) and provides apns-conf.xml in its namespace.

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 5b2cb8d..814a1fd 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -32,6 +32,14 @@ prebuilt_etc_xml {
     product_specific: true,
     src: ":apns-conf",
     schema: ":apns-conf-schema",
+    // A product that ships its own APN database (for example the one of the stock firmware it
+    // runs on) sets the Soong config variable lineage_apn.use_device_apns and provides a module
+    // named apns-conf.xml in its own namespace. Soong writes install rules for every enabled
+    // module, so this one has to be disabled for the two not to clash.
+    enabled: select(soong_config_variable("lineage_apn", "use_device_apns"), {
+        true: false,
+        default: true,
+    }),
 }
 
 filegroup {
